{
  "description": "Sony's global tone curve with the Dynamic Range Optimizer (DRO) off, Standard creative style: knots of scene luminance (white-balanced camera RGB with baseline exposure, through the colour model) to display-linear luminance. The camera look of an ARW shot with DRO on is lowered to it wherever it is darker (crates/engine/src/camera_preview.rs, docs/camera-preview-colour.md, issue #244).",
  "derivation": "Each source raw was paired with its own embedded camera JPEG at the 96-pixel proxy of the per-photo fit (camera_preview::collect_pairs). The pairs of all 12 files were pooled as one model, as dac-cli calibrate pools a camera profile: a colour matrix and hue/saturation table were fitted to the pool, and the tone curve was quantile-matched (camera_preview::fit_tone) between the pooled scene luminances through that colour model and the JPEG luminances. Knots rounded to 5 decimals. Aggregate statistics only, no image content.",
